<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Spree</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Spree is a river in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, about 400 kilometres long, rising in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> near the Czech border and flowing through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lusatia">Lusatia</a> and the Spreewald marshes to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a>, where it joins the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/havel">Havel</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spandau">Spandau</a>. The medieval twin towns of Berlin and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colln">Cölln</a> grew up on its banks, and it is linked to the Oder by canals.</p></div>
